{
  "version": 1,
  "scope": "Static request bodies for ordinary generated AggregateSet product operations on an owned fresh synthetic home. No executable driver, suite, primary data, cloud, or migration.",
  "routes": {
    "declare": "/api/schemas/seed-system",
    "mutation": "/api/mutation",
    "queries": "/api/queries/batch",
    "repair": "/api/aggregate/repair",
    "finalize": "/api/aggregate/finalize",
    "flush": "/api/db/flush"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Submit aggregate_set only through /api/mutation. The batch mutation route refuses this sidecar.",
    "Declare all three schemas before the first mutation. Keep the returned canonical schema identities in the receipt; substitute them if the ordinary name resolver requires them.",
    "Read the current summary guard token after a3. Replace $CURRENT_SUMMARY_GUARD_TOKEN in repair before the request.",
    "Replace $REPAIR_TOKEN in finalize with repair_token returned by the successful repair.",
    "Read all five exact records in one query batch after each successful mutation and after flush/reopen. The b source/member are absent before b5.",
    "A logical removal writes a live source amount0 with contribution total0. Do not use physical Delete or Purge for an enrolled source.",
    "Reopen means stop and restart only the owned synthetic node through its supported command, then repeat the same query batch.",
    "Repeating an HTTP request creates a new signed mutation. It is not mutation-log replay.",
    "Exact signed replay is outside this input artifact. The guarded local proof-engine export/replay endpoints need separate explicit operational setup."
  ],
